  Trigon needed the gotham hallucination  for his plan to work i offered you a  friend a path  they wound down many roads but  ultimately he chose his own way the  season's 7th episode ended with dick  burning his Robin suit symbolizing his  rejection of the darker urges he faced  going after his parents killer  Trigon needed to drag dick back down to  that dark place and the Gotham  hallucination was his way of doing it he  pushed him to the point of committing  one of the darkest acts he could imagine  killing his own mentor dick didn't  really kill Batman but it felt real to  him and that was enough once he stepped  over that line he opened the door for  trigons influence at the end of episode  10 Corey and Donna Troy both try to  follow dick into the house where Trigon  was summoned but they're blocked by an  invisible barrier only dick is allowed  to pass through so why did Trigon want  Grayson and none of the others why  possess him rather than kill him Titans  showrunner Greg Walker told TV Line the  Trigon let's stick into the house  specifically to turn him to his side and  the reason why quote has a lot to do  with trigons plan for Rachel it suggests  that Trigon needs more from his daughter  than to simply have her bring him into  the world whatever his master plan is  this is only the beginning in the  season's second-to-last episode we  learned that angela is just as committed  to bringing Trigon into the world as her  former captors work she doesn't switch  sides she was working with Trigon all  along who's this  Rachel's mother paler cozy the reveal  begs the question of why Angela was  being held in the asylum the Titans  freed her from in the season seventh  episode it could be that making Angela  appear to be a prisoner was all a part  of the plan  giving the Titans a reason to trust her  when it turns out they really shouldn't  episode 8 of Titans  ends with Rachel restoring Corey's lost  memories which turns out to be a bad  idea when Corey then attacks her Corey  remembers that she's an alien from the  planet tamarin  sent to earth for the express purpose of  killing Rachel in order to stop her from  summoning Trigon but by season's end  rachel has successfully brought Trigon  into the world in a way the damage is  done even if Corey wanted to kill Rachel  what would be the point maybe now she  won't have to and can use her formidable  powers to fight Trigon instead for the  most part the real beast boy appears to  be absent from the finale but his  presence can still be felt in dicks  hallucination  shortly before dick leaves for Gotham  and his vision his son gives him his  favorite toy a stuffed tiger to protect  him on his journey the tiger was a gift  from gar which is more than just on  brand for the beast boy  it could also have a deeper meaning it  could be that gar now has some kind of  psychic connection with dick acting as  an antidote of sorts to trigons  influence it might be just the sign dick  needs to snap back to reality in season  2 episode 9 focuses on Hank and Dawn aka  Hawk and of showing us their origin  story as dawn recovers from her fight  with the nuclear family but their  flashbacks are curiously interrupted by  calls for help from Rachel which seemed  to be intruding before they ever met her  in real life what's going on why did  Rachel send her messages into the past  and how did she do it in the comics it  was shown as early as her first  appearance that Rachel's psychic powers  could play havoc with time it seems  likely that the same thing is happening  in Titans and she might not even know  she's doing it either way the hero  seemed to take notice of her cries for  help when dawn wakes up in the hospital  she tells Hank they need to go find  Jason tie with one Robin under trigons  control maybe teaming up with the second  one can help turn things around the last  moments of the season finale featured  the potential introduction of two more  DC heroes and they might just change the  show's whole dynamic the scene features  a naked figure hidden in shadows raging  through Cadmus laboratories in  Metropolis with dead  or dying scientists sprawled out across  the floor as the man opens up a cage to  free a dog he shows a telltale s symbol  just before the screen goes black the  dog's eyes glow bright red it's all but  certain that the naked man and his dog  are none other than Superboy and Krypto  while DC comics have had multiple  characters with the name of Superboy one  of them was con el a clone of Superman  developed by Cadmus labs how would he  and Krypto play into season 2 that's  still a mystery one that will probably  have to wait until dick is back on the  side of the light check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite stuff  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

